          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The opening and closing of stomata are due to changes in environmental conditions. Hydrogen ions (H<sup>+</sup>) and potassium ions (K<sup>+</sup>) are involved in the opening of stomata.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 21
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Describe how hydrogen ions and potassium ions are involved in the opening of a stoma.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "14.2(3)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
